## Projection data shape it returns (ObjectView)

```
{
  id: string,                 // site slug, e.g. "happy-place"
  schema: string,             // "ping.social.business@1"
  name: string,               // business title from the projection
  category: string | null,    // derived from keywords
  locationLabel: string | null,
  summary: string,            // business description from the projection
  media: ObjectMediaView[],   // authorized-only, from src/fyd/media/manifests/<slug>.json
  services: ObjectServiceView[], // STRUCTURED service objects linked by active
                              // provides/offers relationships (see below)
  serviceArea: string[],
  contact: { phone, email, website, locality, addressVisibility },
  capabilities: ObjectCapability[],  // ask/follow/like always; call/email/website when present
  provenance: { kind, ref, derivedAt, label },
  ownerUpdatedAt: string | null,     // from the owner store
  sampleQuestions: string[3],
}

ObjectServiceView = { id, name, basis: "structured" | "owner",
                      basisLabel, visible }
```

Services are structured PING service objects (`ping.social.service@1`),
selected exactly like the site generator: relationship
`subject=business.id, predicate in (provides, offers), status=active`,
target `visibility=public`, sorted by object id. Service id = the PING
object id (stable, deterministic). No prose parsing at runtime; the
ingestion fixtures are test-only. Ask FYD reads the same objects
(ask-composer relatedServices filter), so all three surfaces agree.

